# Architecture

## Component-based work

- Build UI as small, reusable components under `components/`.
- Pages (`app/**/page.tsx`) only compose/import components — no large inline UI, charts, or forms in pages.
- Pages may import from `components/` and `data/` only (plus Next.js/React primitives).

## Data layer (`data/`)

- All API fetching and data access lives in `data/` (e.g. `data/courses.ts`, `data/dashboard.ts`).
- `data/` modules only fetch/transform API data and export typed helpers — no JSX.
- Pages call `data/` to load data, then pass results as props to components.
- Components must not call `fetch` or talk to APIs directly.
- Do **not** use a source folder named `out/` — Next.js reserves `/out/` for static export (and it is gitignored).

```tsx
// ✅ page.tsx
import { getCourses } from "@/data/courses";
import { CourseList } from "@/components/courses/course-list";

export default async function CoursesPage() {
  const courses = await getCourses();
  return <CourseList courses={courses} />;
}

// ❌ page with inline fetch + big markup
// ❌ component that fetch()es its own data
```

## Folder sketch

```
app/           # routes/pages only — thin composition
components/    # UI building blocks
data/          # API fetch + data helpers only
```
